{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268957,"nonce":"OzB4EZMGvymE0J+9Vn5ILPrlQDE=","title":"Python: raytrace's values go dynamic at class sets, None-able numbers and tuples","message":"raytrace's `Vector`/`Point` fields, `Ray`'s fields and most of its locals are `Object`. Each of these was a separate way a value went dynamic, and each is fixed here:\n\n- An operator on a class set (`Point.__sub__` returns Vector or Point) boxed both operands and went through the hooks. That also held both classes, which re-opened their dunders. Operators on a class-set operand now dispatch on its class, forward or reflected, through each class's method; a class without one raises Python's TypeError. Inference types the result as the join of the members' methods, and the call sites record each member's method.\n- A tuple field of class-set type was stored boxed, so `(o, s)` pairs held the classes and allocated per field. Tuples now hold a class set by address (`Field::Instances`), boxing through `zb_hook_box_instance` and reading back through the set's unboxer.\n- `canvas.plot(x, y, *colour)` with `colour` not yet typed in the first round made every parameter `Object` for good. A starred value still untyped now records nothing until it is typed.\n- A tuple literal and the join of two tuples took each field's boxed view, so `(0,0,0)` against `(r, g, b)` floats, or `(o, t, s)` with `t` a `Num`, became `Object` fields. Fields now hold Nums and join with the Num join.\n- `min(1, x)` with `x` a `Num(int|float)` was `Object`. It is now the Num join of the arguments.\n- Arithmetic on a `Num` that may be None (`t` from `firstIntersection` is float-or-None) went dynamic. The numbers are now computed on; a None operand goes to `zb_any_arith`, which raises CPython's exact TypeError.\n- Lists of tuples whose fields differ only in which numbers they hold now join as `number_list_join` joins lists of numbers, with the same check that the callee only reads the list.\n- `isinstance(v, C)` on a class-set value is fixed (dbe4425).\n\nThe type trace now names the first site a re-reading hold came from, and the round trace shows the type a call passed.\n\nAll kernels check. The suite total is 1.005 (crypto_pyaes, telco and richards move ±10% run to run with no type change).\n\nraytrace itself is not typed yet. Even with `firstIntersection` rewritten to avoid None-or-tuple, its later outer rounds start with intersection results typed `Object`, carried over from the previous round's settled signatures. A list parameter joined with that stale value (`List(Tuple(Classes, Object, Class))` against the later `Num(float|None)` field) stays `Object`, and Vector/Point follow through `Ray.pointAtTime`. A tuple-or-None type for `firstIntersection`'s own result is also owed.","files":null}]}